<title>UK: British Energy to announce cost cuts Oct 9.</title>
<headline>British Energy to announce cost cuts Oct 9.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's nuclear power generator British Energy will make an announcement on cost cutting on October 9, a spokesman for the company said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Newspaper reports have suggested the company could cut 1,300-1,500 jobs, from its current workforce of some 6,500.</p>
<p>The spokesman declined to give further details ahead of Wednesday's announcement, which will also be made to staff.</p>
<p>British Energy has said in the run-up to its privatisation in July that it intended to improve operational performance of stations and make further cuts in unit operating costs where possible.</p>
<p>It runs eight nuclear plants in Scotland and Wales.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
